@format 1
@id section-creation.common.keyboard-shortcuts
@title Keyboard shortcuts
@section Section creation
@area Common
@entry window-key,viewer-key
@summary Map the two keyboard-event surfaces that resolve configurable Split section-creation bindings before dispatching Add, Start, Split, or End commands.
@related section-creation.add-at-cursor, section-creation.set-start-creates-section, section-creation.set-end-creates-section, section-creation.split-selected-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag creation
@tag shortcut

@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias binding = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LBinding
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[window-key] Main-window PreviewKeyDown <input>
- Forward the window PreviewKeyDown event into the shared shortcut-key processor @ window.PShortcutKeyHandle(...)
> key-entry

[viewer-key] Split viewer PreviewKeyDown <input>
- Forward the Flyleaf surface or overlay PreviewKeyDown through PViewerKeyDispatch and the window viewer-key adapter @ viewer.PViewerKeyHandle(...)
@ window.PShortcutViewerHandle(...)
> key-entry

[key-entry] Keyboard input convergence <junction>
> input-filter

[input-filter] Ignore text-entry keystrokes <decision>
- PShortcutKeyProcess returns immediately when the original source is inside a text-entry control; otherwise it continues with shortcut resolution @ window.PShortcutKeyProcess(...)
? "Text-entry control" > text-input-ignored
? "Shortcut-eligible input" > binding-lookup

[text-input-ignored] No section-creation shortcut <output>
= The keystroke is left to the text-entry control.

[binding-lookup] Resolve the current configurable binding <process>
- Format the key plus modifiers and find the matching token in LBindingCurrent; the defaults are Q Add, D Start, S Split, and F End but users may rebind them @ window.PShortcutDispatch(...)
@ binding.LBindingGestureFormat(...)
@ binding.LBindingTokenFind(...)
> token-route

[token-route] Resolved shortcut token <decision>
- PShortcutRun delegates non-global tokens through PShortcutCodeRead to the active PFlow; only the four section-creation-related tokens continue here @ window.PShortcutRun(...)
@ window.PShortcutCodeRead(...)
? "SectionAdd" > add-run
? "SectionStart" > start-run
? "SectionSplit" > split-run
? "SectionEnd" > end-run
? "Other or unbound" > other-shortcut

[add-run] Dispatch addSection <process>
- Delegate the mapped addSection code to the active flow @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / addSection
> map:section-creation.add-at-cursor

[start-run] Dispatch setStart <process>
- Delegate the mapped setStart code to the active flow; only its new-section branch is in scope @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setStart
> map:section-creation.set-start-creates-section

[split-run] Dispatch splitSection <process>
- Delegate the mapped splitSection code to the active flow @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / splitSection
> map:section-creation.split-selected-section

[end-run] Dispatch setEnd <process>
- Delegate the mapped setEnd code to the active flow; only its new-section branch is in scope @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setEnd
> map:section-creation.set-end-creates-section

[other-shortcut] Outside section creation <output>
= An unbound gesture or a different command does not enter these section-creation maps.
